  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 119 PM MDT Thu Oct 1 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nA roller coaster of temperatures is the theme for this forecast. \nWhile today will be the coldest day of the forecast period, weak \nridging aloft will allow temperatures to warm into the mid to \nupper 70s tomorrow. A mild shortwave will move through the upper \nlevel flow, allowing temperatures to briefly cool down on \nSaturday. Ridging aloft will once again build on Sunday lasting \ninto Monday, allowing yet another rise in temperatures. Monday is \ncurrently looking to be the warmest day, with highs in the low to \nupper 80s. A mild upper level trough will move just north of \nMontana on Tuesday, creating north-westerly flow aloft through the\nrest of the forecast period. This will allow temperatures to \nrelatively stabilize, with highs in the mid to upper 70s Tuesday \nthrough the rest of the work week. While this forecast period is \nexpected to remain dry, the next chance for precipitation may be next\nweekend, as a more robust upper level trough and increased \nmoisture aloft moves in. \n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nThe weather during this forecast period is expected to be mild, \nwith the potential for record high temperatures and fire weather \nconcerns on Monday being the biggest impact. -Dzomba",
